<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>This download is NOT verified yet: GeoGebra publishes no hash for the file (none was seen in the index of its download folder on 2026-11-13), and a check of the signature is not built, so nothing proves that the file is what GeoGebra published. The shared importer therefore refuses a real run of the cimian recipe unless the override sets cimian_allow_unverified to true (pcman_allow_unverified for the package tool's recipe). Downloads the current GeoGebra 6 MSI for Windows, the installer that GeoGebra's page on mass installation names for many computers (it holds GeoGebra Classic 6 and the Calculator Suite apps). The address is found by GeoGebraInfoProvider (in this folder), which reads the Location header of the one answer of GeoGebra's fixed address and follows no redirect; the Location may be relative and is resolved against that address. The file is stored under a name made of the four numbers of the address. The recipe gives no version label: the importers read the MSI's own ProductVersion. Whether that version has the same four numbers as the address (6-0-936-0 on 2026-11-13) is NOT established, because the MSI was not read. The answer was read from GeoGebra's server on 2026-11-13 and the recipe was NOT run with AutoPkg. The recipe never stops on an unchanged download, so a failed import is tried again at the next run.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.GeoGebra-Win</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>GeoGebra</string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>GeoGebraInfoProvider</string>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>URLDownloader</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>filename</key>
                    <string>GeoGebra-Windows-Installer-%geogebra_address_version%.msi</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>EndOfCheckPhase</string>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
